Node ID=43 the successor
Text=<She does look, and for a moment she is not looking at you at all.> Two hundred years. Then the order stands, and there are still men who wear that, and somebody has been paying for masses I will never hear. I will not give you the Lance, Templar -- I am not permitted and you would not thank me -- but I will not call you a liar again. Tell me what my order has become and then tell me why you have come down here.
Should Have Voiceover=0

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=It has become an order that burns what it does not understand.
Go to node ID=44 what we became

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=It still holds the line. That is why I came.
Go to node ID=44 what we became

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=I have spoken to your Council.
Go to node ID=100 spoke to counsel

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=Later. Goodbye.
Go to node ID=5 Goodbye
Icon=Exit Icon
Is Default Reply=1
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=44 what we became
Text=Then it is an order, and orders drift. Mine was told to hold a relic and it is still holding it, which is either faithfulness or the deepest stupidity in Christendom and I have had two hundred years to decide and I have not. Do not take that as permission. Take it as one soldier telling another that the watch is longer than the war.
Should Have Voiceover=0

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=I have spoken to your Council.
Go to node ID=100 spoke to counsel

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=I will remember it. Goodbye.
Go to node ID=5 Goodbye
Icon=Exit Icon
Is Default Reply=1
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=45 jurisdiction
Text=Your writ. <The sword does not move, but her voice does.> I was tried by a court of the Church in Rouen and burned by it, and I am told that the same Church has since decided it was mistaken. So you will forgive me if your writ does not frighten me as much as you would like. Judge away, Inquisitor. When you are finished there is still an army of the necromancer's dead in the lower galleries, and they do not care what either of us was sentenced to.
Should Have Voiceover=0

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=Then we have the same enemy, whatever the court said.
Go to node ID=46 the same enemy

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=The Church does not answer to its own ashes.
Go to node ID=30 insult

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=I have spoken to your Council.
Go to node ID=100 spoke to counsel

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=This is not finished. Goodbye.
Go to node ID=5 Goodbye
Icon=Exit Icon
Is Default Reply=1
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=46 the same enemy
Text=We do. <A pause.> And if your Church wants this relic to keep it out of a necromancer's hands, then for once your Church and my Council want the same thing, and I will not be the one to tell either of them. Speak to my Council if you can hear them. They will tell you what I am not permitted to.
Should Have Voiceover=0

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=I have spoken to your Council.
Go to node ID=100 spoke to counsel

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=I will find them. Goodbye.
Go to node ID=5 Goodbye
Icon=Exit Icon
Is Default Reply=1
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=47 the lamp
Text=<Everything in her face closes.> He asked me to trust desert magic and I was desperate enough to say yes, and the thing in his lamp heard exactly what I said and gave me precisely that. Two hundred years, Saracen. If your order sent you to take the Lance, you may tell them that the last man they sent took something far worse. If your order sent you to undo it -- say so, and say it plainly, because I have waited a long time to hear it.
Should Have Voiceover=0

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=I came to undo it.
Go to node ID=48 undo it

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=They sent me for the Lance. I am staying for the other thing.
Go to node ID=48 undo it

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=I have spoken to your Council.
Go to node ID=100 spoke to counsel

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=I will not answer for a man dead two centuries. Goodbye.
Go to node ID=5 Goodbye
Icon=Exit Icon
Is Default Reply=1
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=48 undo it
Text=Then find the lamp, and be more careful with your words than he was. It is somewhere below us, and the thing inside it has had two centuries of our company and enjoyed every hour of it. Speak to my Council first. They watched the wish made and I did not -- I was busy dying.
Should Have Voiceover=0

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=I have spoken to your Council.
Go to node ID=100 spoke to counsel

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=I will find it. Goodbye.
Go to node ID=5 Goodbye
Icon=Exit Icon
Is Default Reply=1
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=49 the binder
Text=A contract. <She turns the word over as though it were a relic she had been handed.> You mean that somebody wrote what happened to my knights, and wrote it carelessly, and the carelessness is what we have been living in. That is worse than a curse, spirit-binder. A curse has a caster you can hunt. Very well: you understand the craft that did this. Understand it quickly.
Should Have Voiceover=0

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=It has a caster. It is in a lamp somewhere below us.
Go to node ID=48 undo it

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=I have spoken to your Council.
Go to node ID=100 spoke to counsel

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=Quickly, then. Goodbye.
Go to node ID=5 Goodbye
Icon=Exit Icon
Is Default Reply=1
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=50 she was right
Text=<For the first time she sounds almost relieved.> At last. Everything that has come down that corridor for two hundred years has told me it was here to help, and you are the first one to stand there and admit what it is. The army in the lower galleries would take you gladly, necromancer -- it is short of officers and long of corpses. I am going to watch you every step you take in my crypt, and if you raise one of my knights I will find you wherever the Council has to carry me.
Should Have Voiceover=0

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=I did not come for your knights.
Go to node ID=51 not your knights

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=They would take me gladly. Consider that.
Go to node ID=30 insult

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=Watch, then. Goodbye.
Go to node ID=5 Goodbye
Icon=Exit Icon
Is Default Reply=1
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=51 not your knights
Text=No. You came for the Lance, like all of them, and you will find it guarded. But you have told me one true thing, which is more than the Church managed, so I will tell you one: what holds my knights here is not my doing and not the necromancer's. Ask my Council about the Saracen. Then decide what sort of necromancer you intend to be in front of me.
Should Have Voiceover=0

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=I have spoken to your Council.
Go to node ID=100 spoke to counsel

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=I will decide. Goodbye.
Go to node ID=5 Goodbye
Icon=Exit Icon
Is Default Reply=1
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=52 the khan
Text=The Horde. <She says it the way a soldier says a word she has not been briefed on.> I commanded the army of France and I have never heard of your Khan, which means either he is very new or I have been down here a very long time, and I know which. You have told me that you serve no church and no crown I recognise, and that you were sent to take a relic of my order. There is nothing in that for me to weigh. You are simply a stranger with a spirit in him, and the dead below us will not care what the Khan calls you either.
Should Have Voiceover=0

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=Nobody down here cares what anybody is called. That is the first sensible thing I have heard.
Go to node ID=53 nothing to weigh

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=Then I will take it and go.
Go to node ID=20 demand lance

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=I have spoken to your Council.
Go to node ID=100 spoke to counsel

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=Suit yourself. Goodbye.
Go to node ID=5 Goodbye
Icon=Exit Icon
Is Default Reply=1
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=53 nothing to weigh
Text=It is the only sensible thing in this crypt. Names were what I had -- maid, commander, witch, saint, whatever the year required -- and down here I am a corpse holding a door, and so are they. If your Khan gave you honours, keep them. They will not help you in the lower galleries and they will not offend me. Speak to my Council.
Should Have Voiceover=0

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=I have spoken to your Council.
Go to node ID=100 spoke to counsel

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=Understood. Goodbye.
Go to node ID=5 Goodbye
Icon=Exit Icon
Is Default Reply=1
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=200 have lance
Text=You have it. <She does not reach for it.> Then my watch is over and I find I do not know how to stand any other way. Guard it better than we did, crusader: not with a wall, because walls are what we tried, but by never once letting it out of your hands to somebody who says the right words. That is how it was nearly lost, and that is how I was lost with it.
Should Have Voiceover=0

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=What will you do now?
Go to node ID=201 what now

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=It will not leave my hands.
Go to node ID=201 what now

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=I will guard it. Goodbye.
Go to node ID=5 Goodbye Joan Likes You
Icon=Exit Icon
Is Default Reply=1
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=201 what now
Text=Hold this gallery, as I have held it, until somebody undoes what was done to us or the world ends and the question stops mattering. If you find the thing in the lamp, remember that it hears every word and grants exactly what it is given. Say as little as you can and say it carefully.
Should Have Voiceover=0

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=I mean to find it.
Go to node ID=170 Efreet

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=God be with you, commander.
Go to node ID=5 Goodbye Joan Likes You
Icon=Exit Icon
Is Default Reply=1
